Kindle Anki Port release-entrypoint audit — 2026-08-22 UTC

Starting release-policy state:
  package-and-audit.sh requires QEMU=<fresh run-qemu-smoke output>
  exact-rootfs QEMU must match source commit, Anki pin, canonical PW6 manifest,
  and the exact four ARMHF binary hashes.

Stale entrypoints found after package/QEMU binding was introduced:

1. kindle-anki-port/Makefile
   old package target passed PROJECT/ARMHF/VERSION/BUILD_COMMIT only.
   It did not pass QEMU and therefore no longer matched the production package contract.

2. .github/workflows/kindle-anki-port.yml
   old workflow ran package-and-audit.sh immediately after ARMHF and QEMU host sanity.
   It had no checksum-verified PW6 rootfs and no exact-rootfs QEMU evidence.

3. kindle-anki-port/testenv/scripts/vm-advance.py
   old driver ran package-audit before its optional qemu-exact-rootfs step.
   With --rootfs absent it could still construct a final-looking installer checkpoint.

Corrections persisted:

  Makefile
    QEMU defaults to build/qemu.
    qemu-smoke writes OUT=$QEMU and receives BUILD_COMMIT.
    package requires QEMU directory and passes QEMU to package-and-audit.sh.

  GitHub workflow
    public CI no longer runs exact-rootfs QEMU or package-and-audit.sh.
    it emits an explicit NOT-A-RELEASE host/ARMHF checkpoint only.
    final ZIP is intentionally absent because proprietary PW6 rootfs bytes are not in GitHub.

  vm-advance.py
    no rootfs -> armhf-checkpoint-passed, final package withheld.
    rootfs present -> exact-rootfs QEMU executes before package.
    fewer than five real APKGs or no typed-APKG -> qemu-checkpoint-passed,
      final package withheld.
    only after semantic + ARMHF + exact-rootfs QEMU gates pass does the driver
      invoke package-and-audit.sh with QEMU=<qemu-exact-rootfs>.

  Contract tests
    test_build_entrypoints.py checks Makefile QEMU wiring and forbids a public-CI
      package invocation while requiring NOT-A-RELEASE checkpoint text.
    test_vm_advance_contract.py checks exact qemu-exact-rootfs gate ordering,
      rootfs-absent ARMHF checkpoint behavior, semantic guard, and QEMU handoff.

